hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16173","Affan narrated to us, Khalid, meaning al-Wasiti, narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, the freedman of Banu Makhzum, from a servant of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man or a woman. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of what he says to the servant: Hast thou a need? He said: Until one day he said: O Messenger of Allah, my need. He said: And what is thy need? He said: My need is that thou intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And who guided thee to this? He said: My Lord. He said: Then if not, help me with much prostration."
